    "changelog": [
      "When to Segment: integrated the candidate_rules by naming specific risky surface patterns (noun + immediate possessor/genitive, noun + zu‑Inf, object followed by clause/infinitive, coordinated descriptive noun phrases, proper-name + comma + explanatory pronoun, short predicate followed by relative/completive clause) and instructing that these positions be included as candidates but treated as unstable.",
      "Priority Rules: added explicit lower-confidence categories for the patterns above so cuts that separate a head from its immediate complement or split coordinated descriptive noun phrases are ranked below safer clause breaks; this implements the critic's penalty-without-forbidding approach.",
      "Decision Procedure: added handling for 'reference_suspect' cases: if a local prefix yields an unambiguous, coherent rendering that conflicts with the oracle, preserve the local rendering (flag as reference_suspect) rather than demoting the boundary; removed an explicit restatement about unique numeric tag assignment to avoid duplicating the frozen Output Rules."
    ],
    "next_changelog": [
      "Core Principles: tightened the definition of a 'safe' cut by positively requiring a coherent predicate (a finite verb and its local arguments) in the preceding stretch for top confidence; emphasised preferring clause-complete prefixes rather than enumerating many separate risky patterns.",
      "When to Segment: simplified and focused surface signals. Added a concise list of immediate-followers that commonly disambiguate (e.g., subordinators, relative introducers, explanatory introducers, 'zu' infinitive marker, predicative 'als') and instructed explicitly to treat boundaries before those tokens as candidates but lower-confidence unless the preceding span already contains a full predicate and its likely complements.",
      "Priority Rules: reworked ranking to be driven by a positive test for clause-completeness (subject + finite verb + required local arguments) for high confidence. Moved comma/apposition risks into a narrow, testable rule (comma followed by explanatory/relative introducer => demote). Kept the policy to include risky candidates but rank them low rather than forbidding them.",
      "Decision Procedure: made candidacy pass unchanged in spirit but tightened the risk-ranking pass to apply the clause-completeness check before assigning top ranks and to explicitly demote candidates that separate a head from an immediately following disambiguator token (subordinator, relative introducer, 'zu', 'als', explanatory 'was'/'das' after comma). Kept uniqueness and enumerated ranking requirement; preserved the instruction to preserve locally coherent prefixes as candidates (they may be ranked mid instead of suppressed)."
    ]
